  "question": {
    "text": "$f(x)=\\sin x+\\cos x, g(x)=x^2-1$, then $g(f(x))$ is invertible if",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "hsE0s",
      "text": "$\\frac{-\\pi}{4} \\leq x \\leq \\frac{\\pi}{4}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "UpZlv",
      "text": "$\\frac{-\\pi}{2} \\leq x \\leq 0$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Lltvh",
      "text": "$\\frac{-\\pi}{2} \\leq x \\leq \\pi$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "xq73q",
      "text": "$0 \\leq x \\leq \\frac{\\pi}{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given that, $f(x)=\\sin x+\\cos x$\n$g(x)=x^2-1$\n$g[f(x)]=(\\sin x+\\cos x)^2-1$\n$=\\sin ^2 x+\\cos ^2 x+2 \\sin x \\cos x-1$\n$=1+\\sin 2 x-1=\\sin 2 x$\n$\\left(\\because \\sin ^2 x+\\cos ^2 x=1, \\sin x=2 \\sin x \\cos x\\right)$\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/das8psdkef8Jpeb0nqSuEub-8U_ijwhvC_pHDla6qhI.original.fullsize.png\"/>\nAmong the given options, $\\sin 2 x$ is monotonous\n(here strictly increasing) in $-\\frac{\\pi}{4} \\leq x \\leq \\frac{\\pi}{4}$.\nSo, $g(f(x))$ is invertible in $-\\frac{\\pi}{4} \\leq x \\leq \\frac{\\pi}{4}$.",
    "image": null
  },
